                <pb facs="0353" n="339" sameAs="frus:frus1950v06/pg339"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>The Foreign Ministers of the United States, France, and the United Kingdom met in
                    London from May 11 to May 13, 1950, for far-ranging discussions on problems of
                    mutual concern. These conversations were preceded by preliminary talks
                    commencing on May 1. In addition to the tripartite sessions, United States
                    officials participated in bilateral meetings with British and French
                    representatives. Matters <pb facs="0354" n="340" xml:id="pg340"/> receiving
                    attention included subjects of relevance to the East Asian-Pacific area and the
                    problem of China. Documentation on the London Foreign Ministers Meeting is
                    scheduled for publication in volume III.</p>
            </div>
